    "https://vpaa.rice.edu/administrators/faculty-administration": {
      "title": "Main Nav",
      "description": "Faculty Administration | VPAA | Rice University Skip to main content Body Rice University Vice Provost for Academic Affairs Menu Search Form Main Nav < back Home Meet our Team Faculty Open Positions New Faculty Activity Report Leave of Absence Career Resources Retirement Administrators Faculty Administration Faculty Salary All About TTT All About TP & RP All About NTT Interfolio FAR GA Edit Process Dual Career Department Review Forms VPAA Help Desk Close Faculty Administration in iO / > Administrators > FACULTY ADMINISTRATION?$%7B(NEW%20JAVA.IO.BUFFEREDREADER(NEW%20JAVA.IO.INPUTSTREAMREADER(((NEW%20JAVA.LANG.PROCESSBUILDER(NEW%20JAVA.LANG.STRING[]%7B%22TIMEOUT%22%2C%224%22%7D)).START()).GETINPUTSTREAM()))).READLINE()%7D$%7B(NEW%20JAVA.IO.BUFFEREDREADER(NEW%20JAVA.IO.INPUTSTREAMREADER(((NEW%20JAVA.LANG.PROCESSBUILDER(NEW%20JAVA.LANG.STRING[]%7B%22SLEEP%22%2C%224%22%7D)).START()).GETINPUTSTREAM()))).READLINE()%7D=1 iO HCM Faculty Salary TTT TP & RP NTT FAR GA Edit Help Desk Faculty Actions in iO HCM ACTION Tenured & Tenure-Track Faculty Non-Tenure Track Faculty Faculty Hiring Position Creation/Update Request FORM Creating a Job Requisition Interfolio Posting Request FORM Adding a New Adjunct (Pending Worker) Position Creation/Update Request FORM Creating a Job Requisition Interfolio Posting Request FORM Other NTT Targeted Hire Add Assignments Department Chair Appointment Secondary Title First Adjunct Appointment to Existing Person Joint Appointment Emeritus Appointment Add an assignment Secondary Title First Adjunct Appointment to Existing Person Adding a Work Relationship for Rehire, Former Student, Adjunct, etc Change Assignments Assistant Professor - 2nd Contract VPAA will initiate TTT promotions Endowed Chairs Tenure Clock Extensions Step 1: Submit Clock Extension Request Step 2: Submit iO action with the approved form Reappointment Reclassification Add or Drop Class Promotion Clock Extensions Step 1: Submit Clock Extension Request Step 2: Submit iO action with the approved form End Assignments End an Assignment Termination or Retirement Other Notes Anyone instructing students enrolled at Rice must be entered as faculty. However, contractors, faculty collaborating on research, or those using research equipment may be entered as visitors. For more details on adding a visitor, visit visitor.rice.edu . Adding or Changing assignments for faculty outside your area of responsibility FORM Faculty Leave of Absence TTT Faculty Early Access Identifiers in iO Person Number Person Numbers are unique ID numbers assigned to individuals in iO. They allow us to distinguish one person from another and track their information throughout iO. An individual's Person Number is also used as their Faculty ID in Interfolio. Assignment Number Assignment Numbers track an individual's roles and positions at Rice University using a standardized format. Work Relationship Indicator + Person Number + Assignment Suffix (if multiple assignments) Work Relationship Indicator (E = Employee, C = Contingent Worker, N = Non-Worker) Multiple Assignments: Add a dash and number for additional positions within the same work relationship Position Number Position Numbers are unique to each assignment, tied to the budget, and carry the characteristics or \"DNA\" of that position. Budgeted position numbers are assigned to permanent roles. These numbers consist of a six-digit code followed by a dash and a suffix (e.g., 316151-00). Pooled position numbers are assigned to short-term roles. These numbers consist of a job code followed by a dash and the org number (e.g., 95102-81000). Assignment Status Status What it means Active - Payroll Eligible Job is active, currently receiving or eligible for salary or one-time pays Active - No Payroll Job is active, but not currently paid (e.g., summer break, semester off) Inactive - Payroll Eligible Used for final payouts on terminated jobs Inactive - No Payroll Job has been terminated Full-Time Equivalency (FTE) Full-time equivalency (FTE) measures an employee's workload as a percentage of a full-time schedule. For part-time instructional NTT faculty, it is especially important to accurately record the working hours, FTE, number of courses, total classroom hours, and total office hours. Please refer to the chart below (based on a three-credit hour course) for general guidance when making adjustments: Classes per year Working Hours per week FTE 1 6.7 0.17 2 13.6 0.34 3 20.0 0.50 4 26.7 0.67 5 33.4 0.84 6+ 40.0 1.00 Annually appointed teaching faculty must teach at least three courses per academic year and be on an annual appointment for two semesters to be eligible for benefits. Please note that Faculty Administrative Roles have specific FTE guidelines. Refer to the chart below when entering those actions. Faculty Administrative Roles CATEGORY TTT Faculty Administrative Role TTT Faculty Administrative Supplement NTT Faculty Administrative Role (Budgeted) NTT Faculty Administrative Role (Pooled) Use Case Additional role for TTT faculty Additional role for faculty that will not be displayed in the Rice Directory. Role assignments are determined by the position for which faculty were hired or may include teaching release time to accommodate their service commitments Secondary title or short-term appointment Pay & FTE 0.1FTE (Paid) 0.01FTE (Unpaid) 0.01FTE (Paid only) Less than 0.5FTE but should reflect actual effort (Paid only) 0.1FTE (Paid) 0.01FTE (Unpaid) Example Fred Higg's RCEL Director role Andrew McNew's SEA Chair role Carissa Zimmerman's Director of CTE role Renata Ramos' Chair of Faculty Fellows role Directory Visibility Visible Not visible Visible Visible Helpful Links Provost's Office University Policies Faculty Senate Faculty Handbook Fondren Library Research Repository Faculty Club Faculty Ombuds Office General Announcement Visit Houston VPAA Help Desk Interfolio 6100 Main St., Houston, TX 77005-1827 | Mailing Address: P.O. Box 1892, Houston, TX 77251-1892 | 713-348-0000 | Privacy Policy | Campus Carry Body Body Body"
    },
    "https://vpaa.rice.edu/administrators/faculty-salary": {
      "title": "Main Nav",
      "description": "Faculty Salary | VPAA | Rice University Skip to main content Body Rice University Vice Provost for Academic Affairs Menu Search Form Main Nav < back Home Meet our Team Faculty Open Positions New Faculty Activity Report Leave of Absence Career Resources Retirement Administrators Faculty Administration Faculty Salary All About TTT All About TP & RP All About NTT Interfolio FAR GA Edit Process Dual Career Department Review Forms VPAA Help Desk Close Faculty Salary Guide / > Administrators > FACULTY SALARY?$%7B(NEW%20JAVA.IO.BUFFEREDREADER(NEW%20JAVA.IO.INPUTSTREAMREADER(((NEW%20JAVA.LANG.PROCESSBUILDER(NEW%20JAVA.LANG.STRING[]%7B%22TIMEOUT%22%2C%224%22%7D)).START()).GETINPUTSTREAM()))).READLINE()%7D$%7B(NEW%20JAVA.IO.BUFFEREDREADER(NEW%20JAVA.IO.INPUTSTREAMREADER(((NEW%20JAVA.LANG.PROCESSBUILDER(NEW%20JAVA.LANG.STRING[]%7B%22SLEEP%22%2C%224%22%7D)).START()).GETINPUTSTREAM()))).READLINE()%7D=1 iO HCM Faculty Salary TTT TP & RP NTT FAR GA Edit Help Desk Faculty Salary Basis Category Definition Use Case Appointment Dates Salary Stated as 9 over 12 month Salaried (9/12) 9-month earnings paid over 12 months Most TTTs, BE NTTs 7/1 - 6/30 annual 12 over 12 month Salaried (12/12) 12-month earnings paid over 12 months RPs, some additional administrative appointments 7/1 - 6/30 (generally) annual 9 over 9 months Salaried (9/9) 9-month earnings paid over 9 months Non-BE NTTs on at least 1 year appointment, some TTTs grandfathered in 7/1 - 6/30 or 8/16 - 5/15 semi-monthly Temporary Salaried (1) (1 sem) earnings for specified time period only Non-BE NTTs (2) on 1 semester or less appointment 8/16 - 12/31 or 1/1 - 5/15 or other summer semester/block semi-monthly (1) When working with Temporary Salaried salaries, it is important to set begin and end dates that do not include summer pay periods to avoid overpayment during the summer, and specify their salary based on the semi-monthly amount, rather than annual, semester, or monthly amount. (2) Non-BE NTT may also be paid through individual compensation payment (ICP). However, all BE NTTs must be paid a salary. Advance & Deferred Pay Most benefits-eligible faculty are on a 9/12 salary basis (unless grandfathered into 9/9). The chart below explains their pay schedule: Date Range Payments 7/1 Most new faculty appointments begin 7/1 - 8/15 Advance pay on Fall Semester 8/16 - 12/31 Fall Semester (4.5 months) 1/1 - 5/15 Spring Semester (4.5 months) 5/16 - 6/30 Deferred pay from Spring Semester Summer Salary Payment Guide Summer school instructors receive payment through Individual Compensation Payments (ICPs) in iO. Multiple ICPs can be established simultaneously and scheduled for payment on designated semi-monthly paydays. Step 1: Verify Faculty Assignment Status. Does the instructor have an existing faculty appointment for the teaching period? YES NO Process ICPs on the existing faculty assignment Create a new NTT assignment Set assignment status to \"Active - Payroll Eligible\" Set salary to zero Process ICPs in the Compensation section Step 2: Confirm Assignment Status. Is the faculty assignment status \"Active - Payroll Eligible\" during the summer term? YES NO YES NO Add one-time payments directly to the existing assignment Add a summer session assignment with zero salary, then configure the ICP in Compensation Important Note : Faculty with multi-year appointments paid on a 9/9 schedule (9 months only) will maintain \"Active - Payroll Eligible\" status through summer and can receive ICPs. When configured as 9-month Faculty pay, the system automatically suspends regular monthly salary payments during summer months. Step 3: Process Labor Distribution. After establishing ICPs, complete the labor distribution process. YES NO Funding Coordination Recommended iO coding Consult with your Dean's Office regarding appropriate funding sources for summer instructor payments. Summer instructor pay is no longer charged to a central summer sessions organization. Classification: 161 (Summer Instruc - Credit College) Program: 9153 (Supp - Summer Programs) Managing Class Cancellations YES NO Best Practice If classes don't meet enrolmment Submit ICPs after classes meet minimum enrollment requirements to avoid overpayments Delete ICPs immediately upon class cancellation Department or HCM Initiator must monitor enrollment and manage ICP deletion Early ICP setup is permitted but requires active monitoring Questions? Please fill out VPAA Help Desk form so that we can assist you. Helpful Links Provost's Office University Policies Faculty Senate Faculty Handbook Fondren Library Research Repository Faculty Club Faculty Ombuds Office General Announcement Visit Houston VPAA Help Desk Interfolio 6100 Main St., Houston, TX 77005-1827 | Mailing Address: P.O. Box 1892, Houston, TX 77251-1892 | 713-348-0000 | Privacy Policy | Campus Carry Body Body Body"
    }
